      "notes": "All claims are appropriately tiered and evidence-supported. The E8-based 'measurable' claim about the rebalancing mechanism is technically a description of treaty text/design rather than a measured outcome, but it is factual enough to pass as measurable. The OBR projection is correctly labelled projected. E16 and E34 are advocacy/analysis sources but are labelled projected and not sole-basis for the verdict. The direction 'worsens' is supported by multiple credible projected claims with no counter-claim evidence pointing to a cost-of-living improvement, so no false_balance issue. The preparatory nature of the policy is acknowledged in the rationale and reflected in moderate confidence. No party_blind or lever_leakage issues detected."
